### Pruebas manuales de ms-rabbit-admin (IntelliJ HTTP Client: botón ▶ junto a cada petición)
# 1) Inicia sesión en http://localhost:4200, abre DevTools → Network, copia el header
#    "Authorization: Bearer ..." de cualquier llamada a localhost:8080 y pega el token abajo.
@admin = http://localhost:8083/api/admin
@token = PEGAR_AQUI_EL_ACCESS_TOKEN

### --- Sin token → 401
GET {{admin}}/queues

### --- Listar colas con métricas → 200
GET {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Crear exchange → 201
POST {{admin}}/exchanges
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.reportes", "tipo": "TOPIC" }

### --- Crear cola con TTL, largo máximo y DLX → 201 + Location
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "demo.reportes.q",
  "ttlMs": 60000,
  "maxMensajes": 100,
  "deadLetterExchange": "pedidos360.dlx",
  "deadLetterRoutingKey": "demo.reportes.q"
}

### --- Crear la misma cola otra vez → 409
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.reportes.q" }

### --- Enlazar cola al exchange → 201
POST {{admin}}/bindings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "exchange": "demo.reportes", "cola": "demo.reportes.q", "routingKey": "reporte.*" }

### --- Listar bindings → 200
GET {{admin}}/bindings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ================= Validación (todas → 400 con detalle por campo)

### Nombre vacío
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "" }

### Nombre con espacios
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "mi cola" }

### Prefijo reservado amq.
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "amq.mia" }

### TTL y largo negativos
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.x", "ttlMs": -1, "maxMensajes": 0 }

### Routing key de DLX sin exchange DLX
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.x", "deadLetterRoutingKey": "algo" }

### Tipo de exchange inexistente
POST {{admin}}/exchanges
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.x", "tipo": "BROADCAST" }

### DLX que no existe → 422
POST {{admin}}/queues
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "demo.x", "deadLetterExchange": "no.existe" }

### ================= Eliminación

### Cola del sistema → 409 (protegida)
DELETE {{admin}}/queues/documentos.pedido-creado.q
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Purgar una DLQ del sistema → 200 (sí permitido)
DELETE {{admin}}/queues/documentos.pedido-creado.dlq/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eliminar binding → 204
DELETE {{admin}}/bindings?exchange=demo.reportes&cola=demo.reportes.q&routingKey=reporte.*
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eliminar cola → 204
DELETE {{admin}}/queues/demo.reportes.q
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eliminar la misma cola otra vez → 404
DELETE {{admin}}/queues/demo.reportes.q
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Eliminar exchange → 204
DELETE {{admin}}/exchanges/demo.reportes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Alertas de DLQ activas
GET {{admin}}/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
